nsides to  this render even though it is top end  and I'm actually very satisfied with it  what we are seeing here in front of us  is the ceiling has a very very strange  texture there is no other lighting  except this feature pendant at the  foreground so there's no down lights  anywhere else the strip lighting in the  living room and in the kitchen seems  like a bit of an Overkill it shouldn't  be on during the day it does add a  little bit of warmth a little bit of a  nice character to it but I don't think  it required it personally speaking  overall it is an exceptionally well done  render and I think that again is worth  65 now I wanted to move on to something  a little bit more challenging something  in the actual environment so this is a  small apartment building next to a  Heritage building directly in front of  it starting off with this 30 exterior  render it isn't half bad look I'm going  to give it a bit more credit than I gave  that residential home we have a bit more  context and character they've included a  fence which I didn't model but all of  the extra surroundings like the white  boxes in the background were from the  archicad model I can tell it is from  Twin motion because I know that  background is very very generic very  twin motion the sky is again  exceptionally repetitive from that last  image and there isn't too much  foreground background happening here it  is a very stilted image overall for  thirty dollars because the project is so  big I think it's worth it I wouldn't be  too displeased if I received this image  for 30 or if somebody told me it was  only going to take them an hour to do  overall not too bad now we're moving up  to an image that costs three and a bit  more than the original image so I'm  expecting to see something exceptional  once again we have a lot more going on  and again it is worth the extra money so  looking at this 100 image first of all  they've included the full context again  we have foot Parts curbs Road man